  "lineage": "Dollu kunitha is a drum dance of Karnataka performed by men of the Kuruba (shepherd) community, associated with the worship of Beereshwara. A troupe of dancers, each wearing a large barrel drum (dollu; the generic membrane-drum card stands in for it) slung from the shoulders, beats it with sticks while dancing in formations, slow and fast rhythms alternating under the direction of a leader with cymbals at the centre, and the performance is accompanied by singing.",
